# What the application connects as: a non-superuser role, so that the
# row-level security policies of ADR 0007 apply to it. A table's owner bypasses
# its own policies, so this must never be the owner.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://caballus_app:caballus@localhost:5433/caballus

# What migrations connect as: the owner. Also what the integration tests seed
# with, since seeding two organisations is the only way to prove that a scoped
# query sees one of them.
ADMIN_DATABASE_URL=postgres://caballus:caballus@localhost:5433/caballus

# Which rescue a request is for: the host it arrives at (ADR 0030). JSON, one
# entry per host this deployment answers at, keyed exactly as the browser sends
# the Host header — so a development box is `localhost:3000`, port and all. A
# host nobody mapped is refused with a 404 rather than defaulted, and a map that
# does not parse stops the application serving at all. `npm run bootstrap`
# prints the entry to add for a rescue it creates.
#
# An entry carries what is one per rescue and only a deploy should change
# (#113): `boardToken`, the barn tablet's kiosk token (ADR 0022) — absent means
# no kiosk, the right default for a development box; the tablet is enrolled
# once by opening /board?token=<this> on it — and `"sms": true` for the one
# rescue the Twilio sender is registered for (ADR 0028); every other rescue's
# texts are refused. Generate a kiosk token with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
#
# Where the barn is is not here: it is on the rescue's own row, set by
# `npm run bootstrap -- --org <id> --barn <lat>,<lon>`, and unset means no
# forecast. A link in a text names the rescue's own host.
RESCUES={"localhost:3000":{"orgId":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001"}}

# Error reporting. Unset means no reports leave the machine, which is the right
# default for a development box.
SENTRY_DSN=
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

# Better Auth's signing secret. There is no default: one that fell back to a
# constant would sign every volunteer out the day a real one was set, and ADR
# 0004 made permanent sessions the point. Generate with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# Outgoing mail (ADR 0009). Unset means no transport at all, which is the right
# default for a development box: nothing leaves the machine, and a sign-in
# fails loudly rather than appearing to work. Fastmail SMTP for the POC:
#   SMTP_URL=smtps://user%40heckart.me:app-password@smtp.fastmail.com:465
SMTP_URL=
EMAIL_FROM=Caballus <caballus@heckart.me>

# The Whiteboard Read's model key (ADR 0023). Unset means the endpoint refuses
# in words rather than failing obscurely, which is the right default for a
# development box: nothing calls out, and nobody is billed for a test run.
#
# It is an **OpenRouter** key rather than an Anthropic one — the rescue pays for
# one gateway subscription and this call comes out of it. The model is still
# claude-sonnet-5 and the wire shape is still Anthropic's own Messages API;
# only the base URL and this key differ, both in
# `src/server/whiteboard-read/model.ts`, which is the one module that knows
# either — the way `src/server/weather/providers.ts` is the one module that
# knows a forecast URL. Get one at https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Texting (ADR 0028, ADR 0029). Unset means no transport and no verification at
# all, which is the right default for a development box: nothing leaves the
# machine, nobody is billed, and every send refuses loudly rather than
# appearing to work.
#
# **Two different Twilio products, and the separation is load-bearing.**
# `TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER` is the 10DLC messaging campaign, which carries the Urgent
# Send — a Shift declared Short, and an Announcement whose news will not keep,
# and nothing else ever. The Verify Services carry **sign-in codes**, which sit
# outside A2P brand and campaign registration entirely (ADR 0029): that is what
# keeps a STOP on the notification campaign, or a tripped kill switch, from
# locking the roster out of the application.
#
# **Two Verify Services, not one.** `TWILIO_VERIFY_SERVICE_SID` is the login
# door; `TWILIO_VERIFY_CHANGE_SERVICE_SID` is `/me/mobile`. A code issued
# against one cannot be checked against the other, at the vendor — which is
# Verify's spelling of the `change-email-otp-` separation ADR 0027 built for the
# address. Creating a second Service in the Twilio console is free and takes a
# minute; both are required together, because falling back to one for both
# purposes would fail on the day somebody changed their number rather than at
# boot.
#
# Twilio's test credentials and magic numbers charge nothing and reach no
# carrier, and are the documented development path (ADR 0028) — they are these
# same variables with different values.
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER=
TWILIO_VERIFY_SERVICE_SID=
TWILIO_VERIFY_CHANGE_SERVICE_SID=
